# @podlite/formula

=head1 Upcoming

=head1 0.0.65

=item React 19 is accepted as a peer: C<react> and C<react-dom> are C<^16.0.0 || ^17.0.0 || ^18 || ^19>

=item the formula component names its return type, so its declaration reads the same with the types of React 16 to 19

=item MathJax is loaded at version 3.2.2, not the latest 3.x, with the C<integrity> hash of its file and C<crossorigin="anonymous">. CHTML and SVG each load their own file

=item C<setMathJaxSource({ chtml, svg })> sets where MathJax comes from. A source replaces the previous one whole, so a source without its own C<integrity> is loaded unchecked. The source is read when the script is added, so set it before the first formula

=item a formula whose MathJax did not load, or which MathJax could not convert, shows its source as text in its usual place instead of an empty box

=item a configuration of MathJax the application sets in C<window.MathJax> before any script is kept, and the script is loaded; the formulas used to stay empty

=item a script of MathJax already on the page, with the id C<mathjax-script> or C<MathJax-script>, is waited for; one without an C<onload> handler used to throw

=item C<integrity> covers the first script only. Fonts and extensions MathJax loads itself come from the same pinned version without a hash; to control them, host MathJax and point C<setMathJaxSource> at it

=item C<react-is> is no longer a dependency or a peer: the package does not load it

=head1 0.0.58

=item the package no longer ships C<esm/default.css>, which the export map never opened; the style is taken as C<@podlite/formula/default.css> or C<@podlite/formula/lib/default.css>

=head1 0.0.53

=item a hidden formula shows its source masked and is not typeset; its caption is masked too

=head1 0.0.52

=item the package can be imported from Node directly. The emitted ESM referenced its own files without an extension, which the ESM loader refuses


=head1 0.0.30

=item add C<exports> map (with C<./default.css> subpath), top-level C<types>, and C<sideEffects: ["**/*.css"]> to package manifest

=head1 0.0.1

=item initial import
